<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram id="arch" name="Architecture"><mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c2" value="&lt;b style='font-size:24px'&gt;VANTAGE: natural-language vehicle information on an on-device SLM&lt;/b&gt;   &lt;span style='font-size:14px'&gt;High-level system architecture for TATA ELXSI Teliport S4, Case Study 5 (VehicleGPT)&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="8" width="1960" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c3" value="&lt;b&gt;No cloud dependency&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Proof: the process refuses any network socket and name lookup; answered questions inside an empty network namespace on the Pi" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;fillColor=#e3f2fd;strokeColor=#5b8def;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="62" width="384" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c4" value="&lt;b&gt;About 2 GB RAM, 2 ARM A5x-class cores&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Pi 4 (Cortex-A72, 2 cores used): about 700 MB resident, hard cap 2 GB; same code scales up" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;fillColor=#e3f2fd;strokeColor=#5b8def;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="416" y="62" width="384" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c5" value="&lt;b&gt;Under 2 s for common queries&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Pi 4 median about 1.4 s end to end; reading the question is about 1.2 s of it. Some long questions are still above 2 s" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;fillColor=#e3f2fd;strokeColor=#5b8def;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="812" y="62" width="384" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c6" value="&lt;b&gt;Weeks of history, searchable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Seconds 14 days, minutes 5 years, daily forever, lossless archive, records 5 years" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;fillColor=#e3f2fd;strokeColor=#5b8def;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1208" y="62" width="384" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c7" value="&lt;b&gt;Safety functions stay isolated&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Listen-only, one-way. The assistant cannot transmit or write. Pi 4: 0 missed deadlines, 22 of 22 escape attempts refused" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;fillColor=#fde7e7;strokeColor=#5b8def;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1604" y="62" width="384" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c8" value="&lt;b&gt;1  VEHICLE AND SIMULATION: data sources&lt;/b&gt;" style="swimlane;startSize=38;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;strokeColor=#7a7a7a;fillColor=#fafafa;swimlaneFillColor=#fafafa;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="184" width="330" height="740" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c9" value="&lt;b&gt;2  COLLECT: listen-only, one-way&lt;/b&gt;" style="swimlane;startSize=38;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;strokeColor=#7a7a7a;fillColor=#fafafa;swimlaneFillColor=#fafafa;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="400" y="184" width="330" height="740" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c10" value="&lt;b&gt;3  STORE AND RETAIN: real-time and history&lt;/b&gt;" style="swimlane;startSize=38;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;strokeColor=#7a7a7a;fillColor=#fafafa;swimlaneFillColor=#fafafa;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="780" y="184" width="330" height="740" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c11" value="&lt;b&gt;4  UNDERSTAND, SEARCH, EXPLAIN: the on-device AI&lt;/b&gt;" style="swimlane;startSize=38;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;strokeColor=#7a7a7a;fillColor=#fafafa;swimlaneFillColor=#fafafa;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1160" y="184" width="520" height="740" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c12" value="&lt;b&gt;5  USERS AND INTERFACE&lt;/b&gt;" style="swimlane;startSize=38;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;strokeColor=#7a7a7a;fillColor=#fafafa;swimlaneFillColor=#fafafa;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1730" y="184" width="250" height="740" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c13" value="&lt;b&gt;Expected output 2: Vehicle data collection strategy&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;fillColor=#1565c0;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="160" width="260" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c14" value="&lt;b&gt;Expected output 2: Vehicle data collection strategy&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;fillColor=#1565c0;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="400" y="160" width="260" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c15" value="&lt;b&gt;Expected output 5: Historical data storage&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;fillColor=#2e7d32;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="780" y="160" width="260" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c16" value="&lt;b&gt;Expected output 4: Search and retrieval workflow&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;fillColor=#6a1b9a;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1160" y="160" width="260" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c17" value="&lt;b&gt;Expected output 7: User interaction&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;fillColor=#e65100;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1730" y="160" width="260" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c18" value="REAL VEHICLE NETWORKS AND SERVICES" style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;spacing=4;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#b85450;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="44" width="300" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c19" value="&lt;b&gt;CAN and CAN-FD (SocketCAN)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="68" width="300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c20" value="&lt;b&gt;LIN, FlexRay, CANopen, SAE J1939&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="114" width="300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c21" value="&lt;b&gt;OBD-II and UDS over ISO-TP (diagnostic logs)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="160" width="300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c22" value="&lt;b&gt;SOME/IP services, DoIP (automotive Ethernet)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="206" width="300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c23" value="&lt;b&gt;Android Vehicle HAL (Android Automotive)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="252" width="300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c24" value="&lt;b&gt;QNX slog2, logcat, syslog lines&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="298" width="300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c25" value="&lt;b&gt;ADAS events and camera feeds&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="344" width="300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c26" value="&lt;b&gt;GNSS position (NMEA)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="390" width="300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c27" value="SIMULATION AND RECORDED DATA" style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;spacing=4;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#6c8ebf;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="446" width="300" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c28" value="&lt;b&gt;Virtual car&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;a drivable route, 13 injectable faults, procedural dash camera" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=5;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="472" width="300" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c29" value="&lt;b&gt;Life generator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;105 day and 4 year histories on real weather and real driving traces, with ground truth" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=5;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="534" width="300" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c30" value="&lt;b&gt;Recorded captures&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;candump, ASC, TRC, BLF, CSV, JSON, OpenXC, VSS, ELM327" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=5;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="596" width="300" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c31" value="&lt;b&gt;Cuttlefish Android Automotive 17&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;running on the Raspberry Pi 4 under KVM" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=5;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="658" width="300" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c32" value="49 car models: EV, petrol, diesel, hybrid" style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;spacing=4;fontStyle=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c8"><mxGeometry x="15" y="718" width="300" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c33" value="&lt;b&gt;Local one-way pipe&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Windows named pipe or Linux FIFO, no network. Records carry time, channel and bytes with a CRC-32" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c9"><mxGeometry x="15" y="48" width="300" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c34" value="&lt;b&gt;Sniff&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Classify every block from its bytes: CAN, SOME/IP, VHAL, picture, NMEA, log" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c9"><mxGeometry x="15" y="144" width="300" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c35" value="&lt;b&gt;Fingerprint&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Match the identifiers seen against installed decoder files (DBC, SOME/IP catalogue, VHAL)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c9"><mxGeometry x="15" y="240" width="300" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c36" value="&lt;b&gt;Learn what is new&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Read OBD-II, J1939, VHAL, NMEA standards. The signal mapper refuses rather than guesses" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c9"><mxGeometry x="15" y="336" width="300" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c37" value="&lt;b&gt;Decode&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Canonical signals in standard units, events, logs, thumbnails" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c9"><mxGeometry x="15" y="432" width="300" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c38" value="&lt;b&gt;Check the data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Plausible range, redundancy, stale or stuck sensors, CAN anomalies, harsh events" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c9"><mxGeometry x="15" y="528" width="300" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c39" value="&lt;b&gt;Detect vehicle type&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;EV, petrol, diesel or hybrid, read from the data" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c9"><mxGeometry x="15" y="624" width="300" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c40" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c33" target="c34"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c41" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c34" target="c35"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c42" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c35" target="c36"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c43" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c36" target="c37"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c44" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c37" target="c38"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c45" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c38" target="c39"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c46" value="&lt;b&gt;Single-writer runtime&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;One process writes. Everyone else has a read-only handle" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="15" y="48" width="300" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c47" value="&lt;b&gt;Seconds&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;14 days" style="shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=12;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=11;spacing=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="15" y="134" width="145" height="96" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c48" value="&lt;b&gt;Minutes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;5 years" style="shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=12;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=11;spacing=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="170" y="134" width="145" height="96" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c49" value="&lt;b&gt;Daily&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;forever" style="shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=12;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=11;spacing=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="15" y="246" width="145" height="96" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c50" value="&lt;b&gt;Records&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;events, DTCs, trips" style="shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=12;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=11;spacing=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="170" y="246" width="145" height="96" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c51" value="&lt;b&gt;Lossless archive&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Old seconds, exactly, hash-chained. Size budget 6 GB, oldest removed first" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="15" y="360" width="300" height="66" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c52" value="&lt;b&gt;Sealed at rest&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;AES-256-GCM on disk. The clear copy lives only in RAM and is wiped at exit. Key from TPM, keyring or secure element" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="15" y="442" width="300" height="84" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c53" value="&lt;b&gt;Live bus&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The last seconds are answered straight from the ingest, before they are stored" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="15" y="542" width="300" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c54" value="&lt;b&gt;Retention:&lt;/b&gt; real-time data is kept as seconds for 14 days, then rolled into minutes for 5 years and a daily tier for ever. The exact seconds go to the archive, so an exact question about an old drive can still be answered." style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;spacing=4;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c10"><mxGeometry x="15" y="618" width="300" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c55" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c46" target="c47"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="867" y="306"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c56" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c46" target="c48"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1022" y="306"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c57" value="&lt;b&gt;Safety guard&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Should I keep driving with this hazard? Decided by rules before and without the model" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="20" y="48" width="480" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c58" value="&lt;b&gt;Pre-parser&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Repairs spelling and shorthand, answers questions that need no model (identity, clock, service record, out of scope), and reads dates, numbers and units" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="20" y="112" width="480" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c59" value="&lt;b&gt;Small language model&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Qwen2.5-0.5B + LoRA, int8 on ONNX Runtime&lt;br/&gt;reads the question into an 8-word meaning frame under a token mask: it can only write ontology words, never SQL, numbers or commands" style="shape=hexagon;perimeter=hexagonPerimeter2;fixedSize=1;size=30;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="20" y="180" width="480" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c60" value="&lt;b&gt;Confidence and ask-back&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Calibrated score: below 0.50 I will not guess, below 0.80 did you mean 1 or 2. Follow-ups completed from the last turn" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="20" y="306" width="480" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c61" value="&lt;b&gt;Typed resolver&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Meaning frame becomes a typed, validated query. No model-written SQL anywhere" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="20" y="372" width="480" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c62" value="&lt;b&gt;Search and retrieval&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Read-only SQL on the cheapest tier that is exact enough: seconds, minutes, daily, archive, trip ledger" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=5;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="20" y="450" width="150" height="128" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c63" value="&lt;b&gt;Trends and anomalies&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Change points, Kendall trend verdict, event rate rises, what is unusual for this car, CAN attack detection" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=5;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="185" y="450" width="150" height="128" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c64" value="&lt;b&gt;Explain the cause&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Why did it change or happen: physics trip model, causal chains from logs, 32 deterministic analyses" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=5;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="350" y="450" width="150" height="128" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c65" value="&lt;b&gt;Evidence and verifier&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Every number is traced to the data (measured, derived or estimated); anything unsupported is withheld" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="20" y="596" width="480" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c66" value="&lt;b&gt;Answer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Plain verdict first, working underneath, scrubbed for the role (location and camera only for the driver)" style="shape=document;boundedLbl=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c11"><mxGeometry x="20" y="662" width="480" height="58" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c67" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c57" target="c58"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c68" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c58" target="c59"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c69" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c59" target="c60"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c70" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c60" target="c61"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c71" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c61" target="c62"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1420" y="620"/><mxPoint x="1255" y="620"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c72" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c61" target="c63"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c73" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c61" target="c64"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1420" y="620"/><mxPoint x="1585" y="620"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c74" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c62" target="c65"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1255" y="772"/><mxPoint x="1420" y="772"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c75" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c63" target="c65"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c76" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c64" target="c65"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1585" y="772"/><mxPoint x="1420" y="772"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c77" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c65" target="c66"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c78" value="" style="shape=umlActor;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#555555;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="14" y="50" width="46" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c79" value="&lt;b&gt;Driver&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Ask in plain words, by voice or text. Plain answer" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#fff;strokeColor=#bbbbbb;align=left;spacing=5;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="64" y="48" width="176" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c80" value="" style="shape=umlActor;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#555555;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="14" y="134" width="46" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c81" value="&lt;b&gt;Service engineer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The working, trouble-code history, checks to run" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#fff;strokeColor=#bbbbbb;align=left;spacing=5;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="64" y="132" width="176" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c82" value="" style="shape=umlActor;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#555555;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="14" y="218" width="46" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c83" value="&lt;b&gt;Fleet operator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Many cars: utilisation, risk, alerts" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#fff;strokeColor=#bbbbbb;align=left;spacing=5;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="64" y="216" width="176" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c84" value="" style="shape=umlActor;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#555555;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="14" y="302" width="46" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c85" value="&lt;b&gt;Validation team&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Evidence pack, scenario replay, fault injection" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#fff;strokeColor=#bbbbbb;align=left;spacing=5;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="64" y="300" width="176" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c86" value="&lt;b&gt;Cockpit interface&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Ask, Car, Energy, Map, Camera, Live. Speed always visible, colour only for meaning. Evidence chips and Show your working. Runs in an app window or kiosk, 7 inch ready" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="14" y="396" width="226" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c87" value="&lt;b&gt;Voice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Wake word Vantage, offline speech recognition, local spoken answers" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="14" y="542" width="226" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c88" value="&lt;b&gt;Feedback&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Thumbs up or down kept small, encrypted and expiring, turned into tests" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacing=6;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="c12"><mxGeometry x="14" y="634" width="226" height="84" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c89" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=4;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c22" target="c33"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="385" y="410"/><mxPoint x="385" y="270"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c90" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=3;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c28" target="c33"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="377" y="684"/><mxPoint x="377" y="270"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c91" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=3;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c39" target="c46"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="756" y="846"/><mxPoint x="756" y="263"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c92" value="read-only" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=3;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c50" target="c62"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1135" y="478"/><mxPoint x="1135" y="698"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c93" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=3;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c66" target="c79"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1695" y="875"/><mxPoint x="1695" y="267"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c94" value="question" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#e65100;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c86" target="c57"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1712" y="645"/><mxPoint x="1712" y="258"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c95" value="" style="rounded=0;fillColor=#c62828;strokeColor=none;opacity=70;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="366" y="178" width="8" height="752" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c96" value="&lt;b&gt;SAFETY BOUNDARY&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;fillColor=#c62828;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="300" y="930" width="140" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c97" value="left: the vehicle and its safety-critical ECUs. Right: the AI. Data flows one way only" style="text;align=center;fontSize=10;fontColor=#c62828;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="280" y="958" width="180" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c98" value="&lt;b&gt;SLM / LLM SELECTION RATIONALE  (expected output 3)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;ul style='margin:0;padding-left:16px'&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Qwen2.5-0.5B with a LoRA adapter: small enough for 2 GB (about 640 MB of int8 weights), one decode of about 8 words per question&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;The model only chooses WHAT is asked (act, concept, operator, condition, comparison, entity). Code does the arithmetic, so the model cannot invent a vehicle fact&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Token mask on the output: only ontology words are possible. Prompt injection cannot make it write SQL or a command&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;int8 ONNX Runtime instead of 4-bit llama.cpp: the Pi 4's Cortex-A72 has no dot-product instructions; ONNX int8 is about 3x faster there, and 4-bit was 2.4x slower&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Speculative drafts verified by the model itself, a row-layout output head, a prompt-prefix state: all lossless&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;85.4 percent of frames exactly right on a fresh question set, 84.2 percent on unseen wording; low-confidence readings are refused or asked back&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Other small models (LFM, Granite, xLAM) were tried earlier and dropped: a frozen model added little over this trained frame, and none gave a better speed and memory fit&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#f5eefa;strokeColor=#7a7a7a;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="1000" width="640" height="318" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c99" value="&lt;b&gt;EDGE DEPLOYMENT, OS AND SCALABILITY  (expected output 6)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;ul style='margin:0;padding-left:16px'&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;One application, four tiers (deploy/tiers.json): edge2g (2 cores, 2 GB, 1 model context), Raspberry Pi 5 (8 GB), validation VM (8 vCPU, 16 GB, 3 contexts), vehicle HPC (12 cores, 32 GB, 3 contexts, 32 sessions)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;A planner reads the real cores, memory and instruction sets and picks the configuration; an autoscaler adds a model context only if it really gains 20 percent or more&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Measured: on a 2 to 4 core board one wide context is best (memory bandwidth bound); on many cores, worker processes scale (5.2 to 12.8 answers per second, 1 to 6 workers)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;OS choice: the assistant runs on Linux (Raspberry Pi OS, Yocto, AWS Graviton, QEMU). QNX, Android Automotive and AUTOSAR are covered as data sources and displays&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Demonstrated on: Windows laptop (installer), Raspberry Pi 4 (systemd service, 2 GB cap), Android Automotive on Cuttlefish&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Fleet hub: 16 different cars into one machine at 1977 records per second, no drops, one receiver restarted without disturbing the rest&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#eef4ff;strokeColor=#7a7a7a;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="1000" width="640" height="318" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c100" value="&lt;b&gt;PRIVACY, SECURITY AND SAFETY ISOLATION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;ul style='margin:0;padding-left:16px'&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Local-only: an audit hook refuses every non-CAN socket and every name lookup; the service unit denies the network; nothing is ever downloaded&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Two domains: the collector domain (the only code that touches a bus or socket) and the assistant domain (model, resolver, SQL, answers). A build test reads the source and fails if the assistant can reach a network, start a process or transmit&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;The database handle is read-only; the model's output is a closed word list, never SQL or a command&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Data at rest sealed with AES-256-GCM; the clear copy exists only in RAM; no core dumps, private files, optional memory lock&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Roles with scrypt passcodes, deny-by-default routes, a hash-chained audit trail that never stores content; location, places and pictures only for the driver&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Hostile input tested: SQL, ATTACH, path traversal, log4j style strings, NUL bytes, 4000 characters&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style='margin-bottom:3px'&gt;Freedom from interference measured on a Pi 4 against a 100 Hz real-time task: worst 390 microseconds against a 1000 microsecond deadline&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#fdf0f0;strokeColor=#7a7a7a;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1340" y="1000" width="640" height="318" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c101" value="Search and analytics criteria: historical events, trends and anomalies are found by typed queries over the tiers; causes are explained by the cause engine (sealed test: 87.8 percent first answer right, 95.9 percent in the top three, 0 percent confident false causes). Protocols: nine families checked against independent libraries." style="text;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#444444;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="1330" width="1960" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>